## Dependency Management

- My project is using go modules.

## Describe the bug

If Bash completion is enabled, and the user attempts to tab complete after a double dash (--), it will execute the normal command action.

## To reproduce

Describe the steps or code required to reproduce the behavior

main.go
```go
package main

import (
	"os"

	"github.com/urfave/cli/v2"
)

func main() {
	app := &cli.App{
		Name:                 "cli_test",
		EnableBashCompletion: true,
		Action: func(*cli.Context) error {
			os.Create("/tmp/cli_test/TestFile.out")
			return nil
		},
		Flags: []cli.Flag{
			&cli.BoolFlag{
				Name: "verbose",
			},
		},
	}

	if err := app.Run(os.Args); err != nil {
		panic(err)
	}
}
```

using the v2 [zsh_autocomplete](https://github.com/urfave/cli/blob/v2-maint/autocomplete/zsh_autocomplete)

